speculation.\n- ACTIONABLE (especially for a preference): store it ONLY if you can name what to DO and WHEN it applies, in the user's own terms. A vague disposition ("be concise", "keep it clean") has no checkable form \u2014 skip it rather than inventing specifics the user never stated.\n- STANDALONE: reads as a general fact, not a diary entry. Strip run-specific handles (branch names, commit SHAs, PR numbers, task/ticket ids, agent or session names) unless the memory is ABOUT that durable entity. A fact that only makes sense as "what I was doing when I saved this" fails.`}
